BEGIN_TEXT
How do you interpret divergence? Think of a hose or a drain in a pool. Does water flow in  or flow out? That's the sign of divergence. How fast does it flow? That is the size of divergence. A \( \textbf{source} \) is a point with positive divergence. A \( \textbf{sink} \) is a point with negative divergence. $BR
Consider both vector fields \( F : \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}^2 \) (left) and \( G : \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}^2 \) (right).
$BR $BR
\{ image( "k1-div-1.png", width=>300, height=>300) \} 
\{ image( "k1-div-2.png", width=>300, height=>300) \} 
$BR $BR
